tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part39.sql:917:-- studyprop and studyprop_feature added for Kara Dolinski's group
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part39.sql:918:-- 
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part39.sql:919:-- Here is her description of it:
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part39.sql:920:--Both of the tables are used for our YFGdb project 
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part39.sql:921:--(http://yfgdb.princeton.edu/), which uses chado. 
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part39.sql:922:--
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part39.sql:923:--Here is how we use those tables, using the following example:
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part39.sql:924:--
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part39.sql:925:--http://yfgdb.princeton.edu/cgi-bin/display.cgi?db=pmid&amp;id=15575969
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part39.sql:926:--
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part39.sql:927:--The above data set is represented as a row in the STUDY table.  We have
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part39.sql:928:--lots of attributes that we want to store about each STUDY (status, etc)
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part39.sql:929:--and in the official schema, the only prop table we could use was the
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part39.sql:930:--STUDYDESIGN_PROP table.  This forced us to go through the STUDYDESIGN 
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part39.sql:931:--table when we often have no real data to store in that table (small 
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part39.sql:932:--percent of our collection use MAGE-ML unfortunately, and even fewer 
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part39.sql:933:--provide all the data in the MAGE model, of which STUDYDESIGN is a vestige). 
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part39.sql:934:--So, we created a STUDYPROP table.  I'd think this table would be 
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part39.sql:935:--generally useful to people storing various types of data sets via the 
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part39.sql:936:--STUDY table.
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part39.sql:937:--
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part39.sql:938:--The other new table is STUDYPROP_FEATURE.  This basically allows us to
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part39.sql:939:--group features together per study.  For example, we can store microarray
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part39.sql:940:--clustering results by saying that the STUDYPROP type is 'cluster'  (via 
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part39.sql:941:--type_id -> CVTERM of course), the value is 'cluster id 123', and then
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part39.sql:942:--that cluster would be associated with all the features that are in that
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part39.sql:943:--cluster via STUDYPROP_FEATURE.  Adding type_id to STUDYPROP_FEATURE is
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part39.sql:944:-- fine by us!
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part39.sql:945:--
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part39.sql:946:--studyprop
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part39.sql:963:--studyprop_feature
