tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part40.sql:456:-- dfeatureloc is meant as an alternate representation of
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part40.sql:457:-- the data in featureloc (see the descrption of featureloc
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part40.sql:458:-- in sequence.sql).  In dfeatureloc, fmin and fmax are 
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part40.sql:459:-- replaced with nbeg and nend.  Whereas fmin and fmax
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part40.sql:460:-- are absolute coordinates relative to the parent feature, nbeg 
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part40.sql:461:-- and nend are the beginning and ending coordinates
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part40.sql:462:-- relative to the feature itself.  For example, nbeg would
tripal_chado/chado_schema/parts-v1.3/default_schema-1.3.part40.sql:463:-- mark the 5' end of a gene and nend would mark the 3' end.
