tripal_chado/chado_schema/default_schema-1.31/default_schema-1.31-chado.sql:4474:-- studyprop and studyprop_feature added for Kara Dolinski's group
tripal_chado/chado_schema/default_schema-1.31/default_schema-1.31-chado.sql:4475:--
tripal_chado/chado_schema/default_schema-1.31/default_schema-1.31-chado.sql:4476:-- Here is her description of it:
tripal_chado/chado_schema/default_schema-1.31/default_schema-1.31-chado.sql:4477:--Both of the tables are used for our YFGdb project
tripal_chado/chado_schema/default_schema-1.31/default_schema-1.31-chado.sql:4478:--(http://yfgdb.princeton.edu/), which uses chado.
tripal_chado/chado_schema/default_schema-1.31/default_schema-1.31-chado.sql:4479:--
tripal_chado/chado_schema/default_schema-1.31/default_schema-1.31-chado.sql:4480:--Here is how we use those tables, using the following example:
tripal_chado/chado_schema/default_schema-1.31/default_schema-1.31-chado.sql:4481:--
tripal_chado/chado_schema/default_schema-1.31/default_schema-1.31-chado.sql:4482:--http://yfgdb.princeton.edu/cgi-bin/display.cgi?db=pmid&amp;id=15575969
tripal_chado/chado_schema/default_schema-1.31/default_schema-1.31-chado.sql:4483:--
tripal_chado/chado_schema/default_schema-1.31/default_schema-1.31-chado.sql:4484:--The above data set is represented as a row in the STUDY table.  We have
tripal_chado/chado_schema/default_schema-1.31/default_schema-1.31-chado.sql:4485:--lots of attributes that we want to store about each STUDY (status, etc)
tripal_chado/chado_schema/default_schema-1.31/default_schema-1.31-chado.sql:4486:--and in the official schema, the only prop table we could use was the
tripal_chado/chado_schema/default_schema-1.31/default_schema-1.31-chado.sql:4487:--STUDYDESIGN_PROP table.  This forced us to go through the STUDYDESIGN
tripal_chado/chado_schema/default_schema-1.31/default_schema-1.31-chado.sql:4488:--table when we often have no real data to store in that table (small
tripal_chado/chado_schema/default_schema-1.31/default_schema-1.31-chado.sql:4489:--percent of our collection use MAGE-ML unfortunately, and even fewer
tripal_chado/chado_schema/default_schema-1.31/default_schema-1.31-chado.sql:4490:--provide all the data in the MAGE model, of which STUDYDESIGN is a vestige).
tripal_chado/chado_schema/default_schema-1.31/default_schema-1.31-chado.sql:4491:--So, we created a STUDYPROP table.  I'd think this table would be
tripal_chado/chado_schema/default_schema-1.31/default_schema-1.31-chado.sql:4492:--generally useful to people storing various types of data sets via the
tripal_chado/chado_schema/default_schema-1.31/default_schema-1.31-chado.sql:4493:--STUDY table.
tripal_chado/chado_schema/default_schema-1.31/default_schema-1.31-chado.sql:4494:--
tripal_chado/chado_schema/default_schema-1.31/default_schema-1.31-chado.sql:4495:--The other new table is STUDYPROP_FEATURE.  This basically allows us to
tripal_chado/chado_schema/default_schema-1.31/default_schema-1.31-chado.sql:4496:--group features together per study.  For example, we can store microarray
tripal_chado/chado_schema/default_schema-1.31/default_schema-1.31-chado.sql:4497:--clustering results by saying that the STUDYPROP type is 'cluster'  (via
tripal_chado/chado_schema/default_schema-1.31/default_schema-1.31-chado.sql:4498:--type_id -> CVTERM of course), the value is 'cluster id 123', and then
tripal_chado/chado_schema/default_schema-1.31/default_schema-1.31-chado.sql:4499:--that cluster would be associated with all the features that are in that
tripal_chado/chado_schema/default_schema-1.31/default_schema-1.31-chado.sql:4500:--cluster via STUDYPROP_FEATURE.  Adding type_id to STUDYPROP_FEATURE is
tripal_chado/chado_schema/default_schema-1.31/default_schema-1.31-chado.sql:4501:-- fine by us!
tripal_chado/chado_schema/default_schema-1.31/default_schema-1.31-chado.sql:4502:--
tripal_chado/chado_schema/default_schema-1.31/default_schema-1.31-chado.sql:4503:--studyprop
