tripal_chado/chado_schema/schema-definition/version-1.3.3.011.yml:4544:  description: "A phenotypic statement, or a single atomic phenotypic observation, is a controlled sentence describing observable effects of non-wild type function. E.g. Obs=eye, attribute=color, cvalue=red."
tripal_chado/chado_schema/schema-definition/version-1.3.3.011.yml:4583:  description: "Comparison of phenotypes e.g., genotype1/environment1/phenotype1 \"non-suppressible\" with respect to genotype2/environment2/phenotype2."
tripal_chado/chado_schema/schema-definition/version-1.3.3.011.yml:4704:  description: "A phenotype can have any number of slot-value property tags attached to it. This is an alternative to hardcoding a list of columns in the relational schema, and is completely extensible. There is a unique constraint, phenotypeprop_c1, for the combination of phenotype_id, rank, and type_id. Multivalued property-value pairs must be differentiated by rank."
tripal_chado/chado_schema/schema-definition/version-1.3.3.011.yml:4735:  description: "Phenotypes are things like \"larval lethal\".  Phenstatements are things like \"dpp-1 is recessive larval lethal\". So essentially phenstatement is a linking table expressing the relationship between genotype, environment, and phenotype."
tripal_chado/chado_schema/schema-definition/version-1.3.3.011.yml:5041:  description: "A phylotree can have any number of slot-value property  tags attached to it. This is an alternative to hardcoding a list of columns in the  relational schema, and is completely extensible."
tripal_chado/chado_schema/schema-definition/version-1.3.3.011.yml:5397:  description: "A documented provenance artefact - publications, documents, personal communication."
